## DESCRIPTION
## Find the solution to a system of 3 equations and 3 variables.
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Linear Algebra)
## DBchapter(Systems of Linear Equations)
## DBsection(Systems with 3 variables)
## Date(September 5, 2012)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)
## KEYWORDS('lines')

# updated on 2022.10.29

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',   'PGML.pl',
    'MatrixReduce.pl', 'parserRadioMultiAnswer.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context('Vector')->noreduce('(-x)+y', '(-x)-y');

do {
    $A = Matrix([
        [ random(-4, 4), random(-4, 4), random(-4, 4) ],
        [ random(-4, 4), random(-4, 4), random(-4, 4) ],
        [ random(-4, 4), random(-4, 4), random(-4, 4) ],
    ]);
} while ($A->det == 0);

$x = ColumnVector([ random(-4, 4), random(-4, 4), random(-4, 4) ]);
$b = $A * $x;

@lines = map {
    Formula($A->element($_, 1) . 'x+'
            . $A->element($_, 2) . 'y+'
            . $A->element($_, 3)
            . 'z')->reduce
} (1 .. 3);

$rma = RadioMultiAnswer(
    [
        ['The solution to the linear system does not exist'],
        [ 'The solution is given by %s', $x ]
    ],
    1
);

BEGIN_PGML

Consider the following linear system.

[```
\begin{aligned}
[$lines[0]] & = [@ Matrix($b)->element(1) @] \\
[$lines[1]] & = [@ Matrix($b)->element(2) @] \\
[$lines[2]] & = [@ Matrix($b)->element(3) @]
\end{aligned}
```]

Use the Gauss-Jordon method to find the solution to the linear system in vector form if it exists.
For example, [`\langle 1,2,3 \rangle `] and if needed,  using [`t`] and [`s`] as free variables, like
[`\langle t,t/2+3,2t \rangle`] or [`\langle t,s,2s-3t\rangle`]


[____]{$rma}

END_PGML

Context('Fraction');    # for fraction arithmetic

# augmented matrix to be reduced
$aug = Matrix([
    [
        $A->element(1, 1),
        $A->element(1, 2),
        $A->element(1, 3),
        Matrix($b)->element(1)
    ],
    [
        $A->element(2, 1),
        $A->element(2, 2),
        $A->element(2, 3),
        Matrix($b)->element(2)
    ],
    [
        $A->element(3, 1),
        $A->element(3, 2),
        $A->element(3, 3),
        Matrix($b)->element(3)
    ]
]);

$aug_red = rref($aug);

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

First, start with the augmented coefficient matrix or
[``` [$aug] ```]

and then perform Gauss-Jordon reduction to get
[``` [$aug_red] ```]

And this shows the solution is [`` [$x]``]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
COMMENT("Solution to the system is a single point.");
ENDDOCUMENT();    # This should be the last executable line in the problem.
